# The product of two intervals with one-limb bounds, without a branch: the four products of
# bounds, each rounded down and up (0 times infinity is 0), the least of the four lower values
# and the greatest of the four upper ones. Not in gen/kernels yet: Clang 18 at -O2 computes the
# scalar code's independent FMAs two to a packed instruction (SLP vectorization), and the
# generator's object-code check, one fused instruction per FMA, cannot count those.
kernel:        interval_mul_1
input:         stored xl
input:         stored xu
input:         stored yl
input:         stored yu
output:        zl
output:        zu
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
ieee_only:     yes
cone_exempt:   the bounds are selected among directed products, and the empty set after an explicit test

(d1, v1) = mul_dir_1(xl, yl)
(d2, v2) = mul_dir_1(xl, yu)
(d3, v3) = mul_dir_1(xu, yl)
(d4, v4) = mul_dir_1(xu, yu)
ma       = lt(d2, d1)
da       = select(ma, d2, d1)
mb       = lt(d4, d3)
db       = select(mb, d4, d3)
mc       = lt(db, da)
l        = select(mc, db, da)
na       = lt(v1, v2)
va       = select(na, v2, v1)
nb       = lt(v3, v4)
vb       = select(nb, v4, v3)
nc       = lt(va, vb)
h        = select(nc, vb, va)
nx       = lt(xl, const inf)
ny       = lt(yl, const inf)
ne       = and(nx, ny)
mi       = neg(const inf)
zl       = select(ne, l, const inf)
zu       = select(ne, h, mi)
